WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.550
Two of us typed the same week's

2
00:00:02.550 --> 00:00:04.150
register into one sheet.

3
00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:06.610
The computer says my class

4
00:00:06.610 --> 00:00:07.830
has twenty pupils.

5
00:00:08.610 --> 00:00:09.330
I have eight!

6
00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:13.520
Today: making names agree, so that

7
00:00:13.520 --> 00:00:15.240
every count comes out right.

8
00:00:16.530 --> 00:00:19.050
To a computer, two names are the same

9
00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:21.210
only if every character matches.

10
00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:25.980
So Amina, amina with a space, and

11
00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:28.440
Aminah are three different pupils.

12
00:00:29.230 --> 00:00:31.910
And in Arabic, one name gets typed with

13
00:00:31.910 --> 00:00:35.430
alif or hamza, with ta marbuta or ha.

14
00:00:36.610 --> 00:00:37.910
Clean in order.

15
00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:42.100
First, tidy: trim the spaces at the ends,

16
00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:44.280
and make the letters the same case.

17
00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:47.660
Then match each name to the class list,

18
00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:50.500
the one right spelling for every pupil.

19
00:00:51.740 --> 00:00:53.780
That class list is your master

20
00:00:53.780 --> 00:00:56.920
list: one agreed spelling and one

21
00:00:56.920 --> 00:00:58.520
number for every pupil.

22
00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:01.300
Everything else is matched to it,

23
00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:02.860
never the other way round.

24
00:01:04.110 --> 00:01:06.570
Python can do the tidying for you.

25
00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:09.980
strip removes the spaces at both ends,

26
00:01:10.540 --> 00:01:12.800
and lower makes every letter small.

27
00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:15.720
Put the clean names in a set, and

28
00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:17.460
each name counts only once.

29
00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:20.560
Prevention beats cleaning.

30
00:01:21.250 --> 00:01:24.070
In the sheet, make the name column a

31
00:01:24.070 --> 00:01:26.010
drop-down list of the class list.

32
00:01:26.610 --> 00:01:28.970
Nobody can type a new spelling, so

33
00:01:28.970 --> 00:01:30.170
there's nothing to clean.

34
00:01:31.370 --> 00:01:31.850
Quick check!

35
00:01:32.490 --> 00:01:37.150
A sheet has Musa, musa with a space,

36
00:01:37.790 --> 00:01:41.090
and Moussa, all for the same boy.

37
00:01:41.630 --> 00:01:43.970
How many pupils does the computer count?

38
00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:47.780
Three: every spelling is a

39
00:01:47.780 --> 00:01:49.440
different pupil to the computer.

40
00:01:50.230 --> 00:01:53.010
Tidying fixes the space and the capital.

41
00:01:53.660 --> 00:01:55.160
Only matching to the class

42
00:01:55.160 --> 00:01:56.440
list catches Moussa.

43
00:01:57.590 --> 00:01:59.810
In the app, two teachers typed

44
00:01:59.810 --> 00:02:00.890
a week of attendance.

45
00:02:01.790 --> 00:02:04.650
Choose how to fix the names: as typed,

46
00:02:05.090 --> 00:02:07.810
tidied, or matched to the class list.

47
00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:10.680
Watch the names counted fall from

48
00:02:10.680 --> 00:02:14.020
twenty to thirteen, then to eight.

49
00:02:15.240 --> 00:02:15.780
Your turn.

50
00:02:16.390 --> 00:02:18.690
Which fix stops new spellings

51
00:02:18.690 --> 00:02:20.070
before they even start?

52
00:02:21.410 --> 00:02:23.590
A drop-down list: nobody can

53
00:02:23.590 --> 00:02:24.550
type a new spelling.

54
00:02:25.310 --> 00:02:27.070
Remember: computers match

55
00:02:27.070 --> 00:02:28.670
names letter by letter.

56
00:02:29.340 --> 00:02:32.720
Tidy, then match to one master list.

57
00:02:33.310 --> 00:02:35.250
And in Python, strip and

58
00:02:35.250 --> 00:02:36.710
lower do the tidying.

59
00:02:37.890 --> 00:02:40.210
Try it in class tomorrow: write

60
00:02:40.210 --> 00:02:42.070
ten names on the board as

61
00:02:42.070 --> 00:02:43.270
different people typed them.

62
00:02:43.790 --> 00:02:45.810
Groups find which ones are the

63
00:02:45.810 --> 00:02:48.090
same pupil, and agree one

64
00:02:48.090 --> 00:02:49.730
spelling and a number for each.

65
00:02:50.430 --> 00:02:52.290
That's your class's master list.
